WEBVTT

00:00:01.220 --> 00:00:03.440
My passionate Idol Activities,

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:06.400
Aikatsu! is about to start!

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:14.070
Aikatsu stands for "idol activities", which include applying for auditions and getting gigs.

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:18.300
We use Aikatsu cards to choose our own outfits and stages.

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:20.800
To performers, these cards are life itself.

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:25.280
And so, I'm continuing to attend Starlight Academy,

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:28.000
a private academy for idols.

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:31.920
Ta-dah!

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:33.420
What's that?

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:36.440
They say that this is a critical step on the stairs to success.

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:39.240
It's a poster for the Pon Pon Crepe Campaign Girl.

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:42.920
The first generation was Kisaragi Kirara-chan, and the second was Asuka Erika-chan.

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:46.380
There are tons of other famous idols who have been chosen as well.

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:47.940
So it's an honor to be chosen.

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:54.180
This was even one of the things Mizuki-chan did after her mysterious year-long break to become famous.

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:55.660
Huh? Mizuki-chan did this?

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:57.860
She was the 12th generation. 
You didn't know?

00:00:57.860 --> 00:01:00.960
Not at all! It's amazing how Mizuki-chan did it too.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:05.960
I love Pon Pon crepes, and if there's ever a chance I'd definitely apply!

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:07.280
Sounds good.

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:09.480
Oh, a reply.

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:15.620
So you use KiraKiratter, Aoi. Is it fun?

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:16.800
You bet.

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:22.740
By writing about all of my shining moments, I can connect with all sorts of people on the internet.

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:24.520
Want me to set it up for you?

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:25.800
I leave it to you.

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:26.980
I got this.

00:01:43.930 --> 00:01:45.360
Hi, signalize!

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:50.700
The answer lies on the other side of the sky

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:50.700
kotae wa motto takai sora no kanata

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:52.590
No, that's wrong

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:52.590
iie chigau yo

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:57.970
I can see with my eyes that it's at the end of the Earth

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:57.970
boku no me ni mo mieta chi no hate

00:01:58.350 --> 00:01:59.760
Do that signalize!

00:01:59.890 --> 00:02:04.940
Something's starting to bubble up

00:01:59.890 --> 00:02:04.940
hageshiku natta mune no atsui powaa

00:02:05.230 --> 00:02:08.900
From the burning power in my raging heart

00:02:05.230 --> 00:02:08.900
sou da minagiru nanika ga

00:02:09.190 --> 00:02:12.440
So I'll believe in the present

00:02:09.190 --> 00:02:12.440
dakara ima wo shinjite

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:17.610
And start today since it's more than a faint desire

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:17.610
hajimeyou tada no akogare ja nai

00:02:17.660 --> 00:02:18.950
Chance for me

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:24.250
Dreams can make even the harshest nightmare pleasant

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:24.250
zankoku na yume ga yume de yume ni narunda

00:02:24.250 --> 00:02:28.460
It's just another challenge on the way

00:02:24.250 --> 00:02:28.460
hora chousen matteru yo

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:33.380
Where are we headed?

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:33.380
kimi to mukau basho wa doko darou

00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:37.130
Into a brilliant hope

00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:37.130
mabushii kibou no nake e

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:44.390
Where do we want to go? Let's go find it right now

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:44.390
nozomu basho wa doko darou sagashi ni ikou yo shuppatsu da

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:47.770
Where we're headed

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:47.770
mukau basho wa mirai no

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:51.650
is into our hopes for the future

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:51.650
bokura no kibou no naka ni

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:58.990
Our destination is the future, the light is our signal Let's go, go!

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:58.990
nozomu basho wa mirai no kagayaki ga aizu let's go, go

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:14.040
Vivid Girl audition? Sounds interesting!

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:17.300
An audition to model for the magazine "Vivid Color", huh.

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:19.800
You'll need good fashion sense to get accepted.

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:20.820
Let's give it a shot!

00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:21.530
Sure.

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:28.280
And done! Aoi?

00:03:28.280 --> 00:03:30.620
Huh? My Aikatsu Phone...

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:33.560
We'll be late to homeroom!

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:39.030
Galaxy! Amazing! It's showtime!

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:42.540
Honeys, I've brought a special strong announcement today.

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:47.740
Somehow, auditions are open for a new Pon Pon Crepe Campaign Girl!

00:03:47.740 --> 00:03:48.940
Yeah!

00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:53.360
This is from the poster you showed me yesterday, right?

00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:56.540
Yeah! Wow, I have to apply!

00:03:56.860 --> 00:03:58.180
I'll apply too!

00:03:58.180 --> 00:04:00.540
Okay everyone, be silent.

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:03.180
The audition will be held in our school, yeah!

00:04:03.580 --> 00:04:05.200
Ichigo, let's do this!

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:06.380
Yeah!

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:13.060
<i>It's the same day as the Vivid Girl audition.</i>

00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:15.940
I can't believe that the audition days conflict.

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:17.060
We couldn't help it.

00:04:17.640 --> 00:04:20.380
Even though we're in different auditions, let's train hard together.

00:04:20.380 --> 00:04:25.080
Yeah. Oh, I need to tweet about entering the Pon Pon Crepe contest.

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:28.040
I should probably say something about applying for Vivid Girl too.

00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:32.180
But still, I don't really get what's so great about KiraKiratter yet.

00:04:32.180 --> 00:04:35.600
It's fine to take it step by step. Oh, look!

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:40.800
You should've gotten some replies too.

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:41.840
Right?

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:49.350
Ah, it's Oota-kun!

00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:54.020
<i>When I saw you trying your best, I also somehow got the urge to give it my all too.</i>

00:04:54.680 --> 00:05:00.640
"I'll be cheering for Ichigo-san to be chosen as the Vivid Girl, and Aoi-san to be chosen as the Pon Pon crepe girl." {I know it's inconsistent, loyal viewers. whatever}

00:05:00.640 --> 00:05:02.740
I didn't think that I'd get this many replies.

00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:04.580
Even though you can't see them,

00:05:04.580 --> 00:05:08.140
doesn't it make you realize that there are a lot of people supporting you?

00:05:08.140 --> 00:05:08.740
Yeah!

00:05:09.180 --> 00:05:13.380
Now then! I've gotten all this power from the people around me, so it's time for special training!

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:14.260
Yeah!

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:29.260
Aikatsu! Aikatsu!

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:25.010
Don't look down, keep your gaze straight!

00:05:32.320 --> 00:05:35.380
Hey, did you know that Nao's on KiraKiratter too?

00:05:35.380 --> 00:05:36.780
Huh, who's Nao?

00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:41.480
Huh? He's the Nao of the rock band More Than True.

00:05:41.480 --> 00:05:44.200
Even though they're indie their concert tickets always sell out immediately,

00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:48.780
and they're fighting their way up the major hit charts.

00:05:49.140 --> 00:05:52.040
Their top hits are "I Want a Bullet to Shoot Through Your Heart"

00:05:52.040 --> 00:05:54.450
and "The Kiss of Alice Blue".

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:03.170
So those two are on KiraKiratter too.

00:06:06.040 --> 00:06:07.930
Ran-chan!

00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:12.420
I thought I told you not to add -chan.

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:15.220
Can we sit here?

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:18.620
I said not to use -chan, but I didn't say that you could sit there.

00:06:18.620 --> 00:06:19.540
We can't?

00:06:19.540 --> 00:06:20.900
I also didn't say you can't.

00:06:20.900 --> 00:06:24.220
Then it's totally fine! 
Come on, Aoi, sit down.

00:06:26.920 --> 00:06:28.420
Thanks for the food.

00:06:30.760 --> 00:06:32.560
You really look like you're enjoying that.

00:06:32.580 --> 00:06:33.720
Really?

00:06:33.720 --> 00:06:36.020
Ichigo's family runs a bento shop after all.

00:06:36.020 --> 00:06:39.100
I don't think that has anything to do with it,

00:06:39.100 --> 00:06:42.260
but watching you is making my food taste better as well.

00:06:42.250 --> 00:06:44.880
Ran, do you use KiraKiratter?

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:45.920
I'm not interested.

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:47.760
Really? But it's fun.

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:51.760
I don't really feel the need to use the internet to connect to anyone.

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:53.140
You're so cool!

00:06:53.140 --> 00:06:57.660
But news travels fast on KiraKiratter, and there's a lot you can learn too.

00:06:57.660 --> 00:07:02.230
I much prefer eating together like this than using the net.

00:07:02.230 --> 00:07:05.900
Are you two applying for the Pon Pon Crepe audition too?

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:11.100
I applied for Vivid Girl already so I can't make it.

00:07:11.100 --> 00:07:12.620
What about you, Aoi?

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:13.530
I'm entering.

00:07:13.530 --> 00:07:15.030
Me too.

00:07:16.020 --> 00:07:21.020
But being the Pon Pon Crepe Campaign Girl is supposed to be one of the first steps for rookie idols.

00:07:21.340 --> 00:07:23.700
That has nothing to do with how long you've been in the business.

00:07:23.700 --> 00:07:27.540
I wanted to try being the Pon Pon Crepe Girl too. That's all.

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:29.140
I'll take that!

00:07:29.140 --> 00:07:32.220
Hey! That's the sweet tomato that I was saving especially for the end!

00:07:32.220 --> 00:07:34.120
I thought you weren't going to eat it!

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:36.960
I'm the type who leaves her favorite for the end.

00:07:36.960 --> 00:07:39.140
And I'm the type who eats her favorite first!

00:07:39.140 --> 00:07:41.720
Calm down, I'll give you my fruit pudding.

00:07:42.640 --> 00:07:44.730
Guess I can accept that.

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:48.180
Well then, I'll give Aoi a piece of my fried pork.

00:07:48.180 --> 00:07:50.480
I-It's fine! I'm full, anyway.

00:07:50.480 --> 00:07:51.480
Don't worry about it.

00:07:51.480 --> 00:07:52.920
I'm not worrying!

00:07:52.920 --> 00:07:54.540
You're a growing girl, after all.

00:07:54.540 --> 00:07:56.030
Do you want me to get fat?

00:07:56.030 --> 00:07:57.240
It's delicious!

00:07:57.240 --> 00:07:57.900
I don't want it.

00:07:57.900 --> 00:07:58.490
Come on!

00:07:58.490 --> 00:08:00.500
Ah, that was so good!

00:08:00.500 --> 00:08:02.460
My tummy's all full!

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:04.040
What's wrong?

00:08:04.040 --> 00:08:06.020
Ran's entering too...

00:08:06.020 --> 00:08:09.360
So Ran wanted to be the Pon Pon Crepe Girl too!

00:08:09.360 --> 00:08:10.760
I've gotta cheer her on!

00:08:10.760 --> 00:08:12.000
That's not what I mean...

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:16.500
I know, but you'll be fine. 
Just give it your all.

00:08:17.900 --> 00:08:19.620
It's like the opposite of usual.

00:08:19.620 --> 00:08:20.340
Huh?

00:08:20.340 --> 00:08:22.680
I'm usually the one comforting you.

00:08:22.680 --> 00:08:23.800
Oh, really?

00:08:23.800 --> 00:08:24.960
Yep.

00:08:26.040 --> 00:08:33.280
Aikatsu, Aikatsu...

00:08:39.790 --> 00:08:45.340
<i>No matter what, I really want to become the Pon Pon Crepe Girl.</i>

00:08:45.340 --> 00:08:47.820
<i>I've gotta gather information on KiraKiratter.</i>

00:08:53.590 --> 00:08:59.680
This is said to be the legendary training done by the first generation Pon Pon Crepe Girl, Kisaragi Kirara-chan.

00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:01.860
It has been called the "Ten Centimeter Universe".

00:09:01.860 --> 00:09:03.080
Understood, Master.

00:09:03.080 --> 00:09:05.500
But what's with talking like a wise old man?

00:09:05.500 --> 00:09:08.940
Aren't you the one who responded with "Understood, Master"?

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:11.660
It's special training that my followers told me about.

00:09:11.660 --> 00:09:13.140
Anyway, hop on up there.

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:17.500
It's high! Surprisingly high!

00:09:17.500 --> 00:09:18.070
Walk.

00:09:18.070 --> 00:09:19.840
Huh? No way...

00:09:25.330 --> 00:09:26.660
Ow...

00:09:26.660 --> 00:09:31.100
The width of the chalk line and the width of the balance beam are about the same,

00:09:31.100 --> 00:09:33.840
but now that it's a little bit higher it's much harder to walk down.

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:34.590
Right?

00:09:34.580 --> 00:09:39.460
The width is the same; only the height is different. We should be able to walk this no problem.

00:09:39.460 --> 00:09:43.700
In other words, one must become able to support oneself in times of necessity.

00:09:43.700 --> 00:09:45.600
Thank you very much, Master.

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:47.600
I'll give it a try next.

00:09:51.110 --> 00:09:55.160
I knew it was high, but this—

00:09:56.460 --> 00:09:58.060
There's no way I can't make it!

00:09:58.060 --> 00:10:00.120
Kirara-chan was able to do it!

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:10.300
Fashion shows are about emphasizing your outfit down the runway.

00:10:11.020 --> 00:10:16.000
And to bring that out to the fullest, you need to pose to show off your curves and posture.

00:10:30.270 --> 00:10:32.760
Ready, Ichigo? We're doing bucket walking.

00:10:32.760 --> 00:10:35.480
Is this from KiraKiratter too?

00:10:35.480 --> 00:10:36.680
It's heavy...

00:10:36.680 --> 00:10:38.530
Be aware of the angle of your body.

00:10:38.530 --> 00:10:40.480
I'm trying...

00:10:44.480 --> 00:10:47.100
Ah, Tomato-san replied really quickly!

00:10:53.560 --> 00:10:55.760
Aoi, isn't this chicken delicious?

00:10:55.760 --> 00:10:56.460
Yeah.

00:10:56.460 --> 00:10:57.300
What're you doing?

00:10:57.300 --> 00:10:59.940
Gathering info on KiraKiratter and the internet.

00:11:02.240 --> 00:11:05.380
Apparently Megu-tan does muscle training every single day.

00:11:05.380 --> 00:11:07.430
I have to start it too.

00:11:07.430 --> 00:11:09.200
Yeah...

00:11:10.180 --> 00:11:13.720
Aikatsu, Aikatsu, Aikatsu...

00:11:16.360 --> 00:11:21.560
"How are you? Are you giving it your all? I'm warming up for my next track meet. Let's both do our best!"

00:11:21.560 --> 00:11:23.200
Everyone's giving their all!

00:11:23.840 --> 00:11:25.340
I'm so tired...

00:11:25.340 --> 00:11:26.700
Huh, what's this smell?

00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:28.480
Aromatherapy.

00:11:28.480 --> 00:11:32.500
They say that the scent of geranium and lavender will get you popularity.

00:11:32.500 --> 00:11:34.750
And what's with all this other stuff?

00:11:38.260 --> 00:11:43.340
If you put something red symbolizing the element of fire in the south, it's supposed to bring you good luck.

00:11:43.340 --> 00:11:46.520
The Tiger Eye is to bring you fortune,

00:11:46.520 --> 00:11:51.180
and the lapis lazuli is to make you smarter and more determined.

00:11:51.180 --> 00:11:56.690
If you use a special decorative plant you'll be able to absorb even more fortune from the power of nature.

00:11:56.690 --> 00:12:01.180
The natural power brings a purification effect, and the flower patterning too.

00:12:01.180 --> 00:12:06.450
The Yin-Yang mark represents the balance of all things in creation, and...

00:12:06.900 --> 00:12:08.880
Is this all from KiraKiratter?

00:12:08.880 --> 00:12:12.220
Yeah! Info really travels fast through KiraKiratter!

00:12:12.220 --> 00:12:14.920
If you ask a question your followers will always respond.

00:12:19.680 --> 00:12:22.100
"Ichigo-chan, do your best with Aikatsu."

00:12:22.100 --> 00:12:24.820
"Aikatsu, you katsu, we all katsu!"

00:12:24.820 --> 00:12:26.970
That's not even a good pun!

00:12:28.300 --> 00:12:29.480
Aoi?

00:12:29.480 --> 00:12:34.480
Aikatsu, Aikatsu...

00:12:39.460 --> 00:12:42.940
It's Satakecchi-san. "I'm doing my best. Please cheer me on."

00:12:51.450 --> 00:12:53.200
It's finally audition day.

00:12:53.200 --> 00:12:53.750
Yeah... {Ah!}

00:12:55.100 --> 00:12:56.600
What are you doing?

00:12:56.600 --> 00:13:01.160
Ran is entering, so I'm not giving up on collecting data until the very end.

00:13:01.160 --> 00:13:04.180
You're asking your followers on KiraKiratter for advice?

00:13:04.400 --> 00:13:05.280
Yeah.

00:13:07.660 --> 00:13:10.260
Do your best with the Pon Pon Crepe audition!

00:13:35.960 --> 00:13:38.090
I need to clean that.

00:13:39.100 --> 00:13:40.920
I'm sorry.

00:13:41.800 --> 00:13:45.200
Do you think you can win just by relying on the internet?

00:13:45.200 --> 00:13:45.920
What?

00:13:46.240 --> 00:13:49.000
Do you think that Shibuki Ran imitates other people

00:13:49.000 --> 00:13:51.180
or relies on objects of good fortune?

00:13:51.180 --> 00:13:54.320
But, but Ran has rare cards...

00:13:54.320 --> 00:13:58.650
If you really want them that badly, then I'll give you some Futuring Girl rare cards.

00:14:03.740 --> 00:14:05.150
Amazing...

00:14:05.150 --> 00:14:07.900
I wonder if you can make use of them as you are now.

00:14:08.260 --> 00:14:09.370
Huh?

00:14:13.760 --> 00:14:16.780
I even got rare cards, but...

00:14:20.290 --> 00:14:23.740
Oh, if it isn't the headmistress. How unusual.

00:14:23.740 --> 00:14:25.740
I wanted to see Ran's performance.

00:14:25.740 --> 00:14:28.180
I'm sure she'll <i>show</i> us an exciting show!

00:14:28.560 --> 00:14:29.800
Just kidding.

00:14:32.160 --> 00:14:33.180
Forgive me...

00:14:40.580 --> 00:14:44.940
We will now be starting the Pon Pon Crepe Campaign Girl auditon.

00:14:44.940 --> 00:14:46.820
Number 1, Yuzuha Mei.

00:14:47.160 --> 00:14:48.360
Here!

00:14:53.080 --> 00:14:56.140
<i>Do you think that Shibuki Ran imitates other people</i>

00:14:56.140 --> 00:14:58.340
<i>or relies on objects of good fortune?</i>

00:14:58.330 --> 00:15:01.320
<i>Do your best with the Pon Pon Crepe audition!</i>

00:15:02.380 --> 00:15:09.380
<i>I couldn't even wish my best friend good luck on her audition when she was right in front of my eyes.</i>

00:15:09.380 --> 00:15:12.320
<i>At this rate, I'll lose to Ran...</i>

00:15:22.230 --> 00:15:26.040
<i>Ichigo, I've been thinking only about myself.</i>

00:15:26.040 --> 00:15:28.740
<i>I'm sorry. Do your best with Vivid Girl.</i>

00:15:45.630 --> 00:15:47.640
This year's bar is set pretty high.

00:15:47.640 --> 00:15:52.120
That's right. Both Shibuki Ran and Kiriya Aoi have entered.

00:15:53.640 --> 00:15:55.440
<i>There's no response...</i>

00:15:55.440 --> 00:15:57.060
<i>I'm sure she's angry.</i>

00:15:58.890 --> 00:16:02.900
"I couldn't respond since I was on the bus. I'm sorry, too,

00:16:02.920 --> 00:16:06.140
for not recognizing why you were trying so hard."

00:16:06.150 --> 00:16:07.460
Ichigo!

00:16:08.080 --> 00:16:12.400
<i>Not at all. I really </i>was<i> only thinking about myself.</i>

00:16:15.410 --> 00:16:19.140
"Do your best! Aoi, I'm sure you can do it! You'll be fine!"

00:16:19.120 --> 00:16:22.260
Number 33, Shibuki Ran.

00:16:23.640 --> 00:16:26.460
Shibuki Ran. Shibuki Ran?

00:16:27.220 --> 00:16:28.670
Here!

00:16:37.680 --> 00:16:38.980
As expected of Shibuki.

00:16:38.980 --> 00:16:40.180
Her sharpness is unparalleled.

00:16:42.180 --> 00:16:44.680
The current leader is Shibuki Ran.

00:16:45.900 --> 00:16:50.140
<i>The highest score... this may be impossible...</i>

00:16:50.140 --> 00:16:52.190
Number 35, Mori Kurumi.

00:17:01.240 --> 00:17:02.660
<i>I can't!</i>

00:17:07.180 --> 00:17:08.460
You <i>can</i> do it! {yeah, emphasis!}

00:17:16.140 --> 00:17:17.460
Ichigo?

00:17:17.980 --> 00:17:20.970
They let me go early in the Vivid Girl auditions.

00:17:26.480 --> 00:17:30.480
I couldn't express my feelings just through KiraKiratter.

00:17:38.540 --> 00:17:39.980
Ichigo?

00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:47.500
Number 36, Kiriya Aoi.

00:17:48.020 --> 00:17:49.180
Here!

00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:32.440
That was a wonderful performance.

00:20:34.800 --> 00:20:35.700
Ichigo.

00:20:35.700 --> 00:20:37.380
Aoi, you were awesome!

00:20:37.380 --> 00:20:39.380
We both put in our best.

00:20:57.520 --> 00:20:58.460
You did it!

00:20:58.460 --> 00:21:00.920
I'm gonna be the Pon Pon Crepe Girl?

00:21:00.920 --> 00:21:01.760
That's right!

00:21:01.760 --> 00:21:03.030
Good job.

00:21:03.030 --> 00:21:04.460
Thank you.

00:21:04.460 --> 00:21:07.520
Too bad, I really wanted to see Ran using her rare cards.

00:21:07.530 --> 00:21:10.480
I use rare cards only when I want to.

00:21:10.480 --> 00:21:12.160
They aren't just things to be used when you're told to.

00:21:16.170 --> 00:21:18.160
Ta-dah!

00:21:18.160 --> 00:21:20.420
I still can't believe it's me.

00:21:21.580 --> 00:21:22.920
It's real life.

00:21:28.980 --> 00:21:31.200
Yes! I passed for Vivid Girl!

00:21:31.200 --> 00:21:32.100
Awesome!

00:21:41.660 --> 00:21:42.440
Who?

00:21:43.160 --> 00:21:45.140
Do you know this Moon-san?

00:21:45.140 --> 00:21:46.700
No...

00:21:47.700 --> 00:21:51.940
"May your dreams tonight be sweet as a crepe."

00:21:52.700 --> 00:21:54.900
Their profile is completely empty.

00:21:54.900 --> 00:21:58.940
And all the tweets are all things like "The moon is really pretty".

00:21:58.940 --> 00:22:02.780
I don't really get it, but is it some sort of special message just for us?

00:22:02.780 --> 00:22:03.460
Maybe.

00:22:04.130 --> 00:22:06.720
Still, those were some pretty words.

00:22:06.720 --> 00:22:10.730
"May your dreams tonight be sweet as a crepe."

00:23:55.640 --> 00:23:58.480
Aoi, there's an underground idol at the academy.

00:23:58.480 --> 00:23:59.620
An underground idol?

00:23:59.620 --> 00:24:01.600
Yeah, she's really cool!

00:24:01.600 --> 00:24:03.560
You'll get burned if you touch me.

00:24:03.560 --> 00:24:04.320
Huh?

00:24:04.320 --> 00:24:05.960
Next time on Aikatsu!

00:24:05.960 --> 00:24:07.460
The Underground Sun.

00:24:07.460 --> 00:24:10.380
Always passionate, Idol Activities!

00:24:11.300 --> 00:24:13.260
This week's Aikatsu Aphorism!

00:24:14.300 --> 00:24:16.900
Ichigo, where do you start eating a shortcake from?

00:24:16.900 --> 00:24:18.260
The strawberry, of course!

00:24:18.260 --> 00:24:21.220
If I don't, then Raichi'll take it from me.

00:24:21.220 --> 00:24:22.300
I get it.

00:24:23.140 --> 00:24:25.920
Eat your favorite food first!
